&gt; You have to really get into the mind of the original developer, and try to guess at why they do things the way they do. Understand their favorite anti-patterns and their tics.

Last week, I saw some legacy code that was:

    if (some condition)
    { }
    else {
        actual result
    }

It took me like 15 minutes to wrap my head around this concept, because it made no fucking sense to me. Why not just reverse the if statement?
